{
 "slug": "test/comparison",
 "about": "Comparing saved measurements: the entries a comparison holds, their labels and range, the mode, detection standing down, the per-tap overlay giving way, each entry's Air/Top/Back taken from its source, and saving and loading a comparison. Each case starts a fresh analyzer (threshold −40, Taps 1) with an empty library and runs its 'steps': the shared steps of tooling/analyzer-steps (settings, setTaps, newTap, guitarTap, advance), and {\"compare\": [files]} (a comparison of those 'files' entries, as a multi-select in the list makes); {\"clearComparison\": true}; {\"load\": file} (loaded as a file); {\"multiTap\": bool} (the Taps toggle: the per-tap overlay of the measurement on screen, on or off); {\"saveComparison\": name} (saves the comparison shown); {\"loadSaved\": true} (loads the last saved record); {\"check\": {...}}. Fields: 'entries' (count), 'labels', 'mode' (live / comparison), 'loadedRange' ([minFreq, maxFreq, minDB, maxDB]), 'detecting', 'multiTap' (the per-tap overlay is showing), 'tapEntries' (count), 'savedComparison' (the comparison is of saved measurements), 'modeIds' (the first entry's stored map, mode display name → peak, by 'peakNames'), 'entryPeaks' (the first entry's peaks, by name, any order), 'entryGuitarType' (the first entry's guitar type), 'savedRecord' (the last saved record — {name, entries} — or null for none added), 'phase' (Swift's raw value), 'complete'. Expected values are Swift's.",
